{
  "id": "m49l1",
  "title": {
    "es": "match/case: lo básico",
    "en": "match/case: the basics"
  },
  "theory": {
    "es": [
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "value": "Comparar por patrones (Python 3.10+)"
      },
      {
        "type": "text",
        "value": "`match` compara un valor contra varios **patrones** (`case`). Es como un `if/elif` más legible. `case _` es el comodín (cualquier cosa), como el `else`."
      },
      {
        "type": "code",
        "value": [
          "def describir(n):",
          "    match n:",
          "        case 0:",
          "            return 'cero'",
          "        case 1:",
          "            return 'uno'",
          "        case _:",
          "            return 'otro'",
          "",
          "print(describir(0), describir(5))"
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "output",
        "value": [
          "cero otro"
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "text",
        "value": "Puedes combinar varios valores en un patrón con `|` (o lógico): `case 'sí' | 'vale':`."
      },
      {
        "type": "note",
        "value": "Disponible desde Python 3.10. No es un simple switch: también desestructura datos, como verás luego."
      }
    ],
    "en": [
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "value": "Matching by patterns (Python 3.10+)"
      },
      {
        "type": "text",
        "value": "`match` compares a value against several **patterns** (`case`). It's like a more readable `if/elif`. `case _` is the wildcard (anything), like `else`."
      },
      {
        "type": "code",
        "value": [
          "def describir(n):",
          "    match n:",
          "        case 0:",
          "            return 'cero'",
          "        case 1:",
          "            return 'uno'",
          "        case _:",
          "            return 'otro'",
          "",
          "print(describir(0), describir(5))"
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "output",
        "value": [
          "cero otro"
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "text",
        "value": "You can combine several values in one pattern with `|` (logical or): `case 'yes' | 'ok':`."
      },
      {
        "type": "note",
        "value": "Available since Python 3.10. It's not just a switch: it also destructures data, as you'll see next."
      }
    ]
  },
  "exercises": [
    {
      "id": "m49l1e1",
      "prompt": {
        "es": "Define `describir(n)` con match: 0 -> 'cero', 1 -> 'uno', cualquier otro -> 'otro'.",
        "en": "Define `describir(n)` with match: 0 -> 'cero', 1 -> 'uno', anything else -> 'otro'."
      },
      "starter_code": [
        "def describir(n):",
        "    pass"
      ],
      "solution": [
        "def describir(n):",
        "    match n:",
        "        case 0:",
        "            return 'cero'",
        "        case 1:",
        "            return 'uno'",
        "        case _:",
        "            return 'otro'"
      ],
      "hints": {
        "es": [
          "Usa case 0, case 1 y case _."
        ],
        "en": [
          "Use case 0, case 1 and case _."
        ]
      },
      "tests": [
        {
          "type": "function",
          "function": "describir",
          "cases": [
            {
              "args": [
                0
              ],
              "expected": "cero"
            },
            {
              "args": [
                1
              ],
              "expected": "uno"
            },
            {
              "args": [
                7
              ],
              "expected": "otro"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "m49l1e2",
      "prompt": {
        "es": "Define `tipo_dia(dia)` con match: 'sabado' o 'domingo' -> 'finde'; cualquier otro -> 'laborable' (usa el patrón |).",
        "en": "Define `tipo_dia(dia)` with match: 'sabado' or 'domingo' -> 'finde'; otherwise -> 'laborable' (use the | pattern)."
      },
      "starter_code": [
        "def tipo_dia(dia):",
        "    pass"
      ],
      "solution": [
        "def tipo_dia(dia):",
        "    match dia:",
        "        case 'sabado' | 'domingo':",
        "            return 'finde'",
        "        case _:",
        "            return 'laborable'"
      ],
      "hints": {
        "es": [
          "case 'sabado' | 'domingo' combina ambos."
        ],
        "en": [
          "case 'sabado' | 'domingo' combines both."
        ]
      },
      "tests": [
        {
          "type": "function",
          "function": "tipo_dia",
          "cases": [
            {
              "args": [
                "sabado"
              ],
              "expected": "finde"
            },
            {
              "args": [
                "domingo"
              ],
              "expected": "finde"
            },
            {
              "args": [
                "lunes"
              ],
              "expected": "laborable"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    }
  ]
}